<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.210
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.590
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.090
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:14.590
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.590
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:27.060
<b>Battle God Ghingnham</b>

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.620
This construct is Mistletoe! Please cease your combat status!

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:52.550
Mahiroo Squadron, please relay the following message to Gym Ghingnham!

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:54.760
I am Harry Ord...

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:58.720
...and I have rescued Queen Dianna from the Militia's spacecraft!

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.140
Is that the Royal Guard's Harry?

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:07.520
Really, now?

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:17.440
All these Mechanical Dolls suddenly appeared all at once. Why do you think that is?

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:18.530
Forgive me.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.030
What is it you've done?

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:23.830
It's because I have to save Dianna that you're in this position.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:29.920
It's fine. Queen Dianna and my sister are essentially the same person. I can't hate her completely now.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:54.820
This place is Mistletoe's control center.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:57.150
Oh? THIS is it?

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:01.160
Did Queen Dianna's ancestors use this location to improve the quality of agriculture...

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.320
...and allow for better crop production in space?

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.830
That's correct.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:09.750
Since plants require water and insects to thrive, it was a massive undertaking.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:12.920
Looks like this tree is still alive...

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:21.550
Agrippa and Ghingnham are said to be the eagles whom are watching over the goddess' crown.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.140
Each person has their own purpose.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:28.140
Long ago, I'd left the Kafka family on earth...

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:32.140
Your ancestors personally wished to settle on Earth and live there.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:37.230
...That's what we've needed to hear you say!

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:41.240
Please forgive me for neglecting the House of Kafka.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:42.660
Your Majesty!

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:44.950
Will you be able to restore it?

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:47.120
Not entirely.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:50.120
- Please flip that switch for me.
- Uh, sure.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.540
Looks like it worked. That's one of the Mahiroo Squadron's grunts!

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.630
But, we don't know his position, do we?

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:01.050
Let's see... it's somewhere around this pathway.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.420
That's nearby.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:12.850
Don't move!

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:16.810
What are you trying to pull? I already know you aren't here with anyone else!

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:20.650
Don't underestimate me. I'm one of the men chosen for the Ghingnham Squadron.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:24.240
It'd be pointless to argue with a bunch of terran barbarians like...

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:27.450
Let's go!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.450
- Queen Dianna...
- Right!

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:35.250
You don't think they destroyed our FLAT, do you?

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:38.340
That guy didn't look like he'd be that thorough.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:39.550
It shouldn't be a problem.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:41.260
I sure hope not.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:48.350
No way! He even left us his OWN Mobile Suit!

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.850
Let's take it!

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.850
You two have earned this luck!

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:55.850
I see...

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:59.520
This one seems to be somewhat older than a FLAT...

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.650
Muron, did you get the Queen aboard?

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:11.540
Yup. As for you, make sure you cover us. We can't let anything happen to the Queen.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.040
Yeah, yeah, I know!

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:40.810
We'll have to make it past all of them...

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:44.150
Could you attempt to contact the Ghingnham squadron, Muron?

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:47.740
Not a chance. They intend to take your life, my Queen.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:49.450
Negotiations with them would be impossible.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.120
Why the sudden stop?

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:58.040
I can hear combat nearby.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.050
The enemy!

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:07.050
Hold off for a moment...

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.630
There's also a High Heel.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:09.840
It's the Mustache?

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.050
Is that you, Loran?

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:19.520
Loran, I'm glad you made it here. This is Dianna Soriel.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.940
You haven't been hurt, have you? Are you cold?

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:26.030
Can we really trust these people, Captain?

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:29.320
The Mustache and the little ball are also my subordinates.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:32.830
They're just like yourself and the former Kafka family.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:36.830
But isn't the White Doll also that "Gundam"?

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.540
You know about that?

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:46.340
Well, didn't the Moonrace, no... all spacenoids once consider it an accursed Mobile Suit, Highness?

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:50.220
Cancer Kafka, a mobile suit is simply a tool.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.850
The key lies in how we use them.

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:55.850
So I ask you to please put your trust in that boy.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.110
Let's escape from here, Loran.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:17.330
If the atomic bomb in your chest were to detonate, we'd all be killed.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.540
I understand.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:28.340
So If you take me to see Midgard as Dianna, I need to find an opportunity to take down Agrippa.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.840
The factor in question is Gym Ghingnham.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:33.840
He may prevent you from directly reaching Agrippa.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:36.640
In your opinion, Lieutenant Harry...

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:41.640
...Am I, Kihel Heim, unworthy of playing Queen Dianna's double?

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:45.810
In what way do you mean? I think you're a quite suitable woman...

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:49.530
I... also like you, Sir Harry.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.030
I am honored.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:54.820
This isn't how things were meant to be, is it, Harry Ord?

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:57.450
Since l'm the Commander of the Royal Guard...

00:07:57.450 --> 00:08:00.620
Queen Dianna is the only one whom I am allowed to hold in my heart.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:03.420
- Sir Harry...
- And so, I can't let myself be moved by...

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:04.630
Harry!

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:09.050
Just tell me that you love me!

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:12.340
After that, I'll do what you wish without question, including assassinating Agrippa.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.430
Kihel Heim...

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:23.440
You are free to strike me, if you desire.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:35.320
I wish for you to become Dianna's shield.

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:44.250
And all the same, I'll love you as best I can, though it may not be a love worthy of you.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:07.730
And our rotational axis... All clear!

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.440
Adjust the altitude to match port side.

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:14.820
The vibrations stop, and gravity kicks in.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.320
Have we arrived on the moon already?

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.820
No, it's gravity from the inertia.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:20.120
What would you like next?

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.240
Send a mechanical doll to investigate.

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:24.450
If we don't want the Mahiroo Team to get us...

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:26.920
We'll have to attempt to sneak into Mistletoe, instead.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:28.420
Alright, we're in place.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:31.630
"Armadillo", I want you to check around that hatch for us.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:34.630
There should be a lock bar to the left or right of the dock.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:36.930
You need to find a way to move those, first.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:39.340
You may return back here if it gets too scary out there.

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:45.230
It's not a problem. Space Suits and these "Armadillos" aren't nearly as tricky to use as a Kapool.

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:46.350
Great.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:48.850
Armadillo, Launching!

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:57.240
Oh man... The stars are moving now.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:58.740
Is that it over there?

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:15.840
There's the keylock!

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:20.840
Opened!

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.640
Is the port opening?

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:27.730
Yes. It appears the systems are still active.

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:49.620
Let go of me!

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:54.340
They gave us specific orders to wait while Harry is in the Aspite.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:56.420
I'm itching for some combat!

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:59.930
Well, the Royal Guard's actions might determine if the General orders us to commence operation E Minor.

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:03.550
E Minor... then it will wait.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:12.230
Her Majesty, Dianna Soriel... Salute!

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:19.440
So what you're saying is that she's not the real Dianna.

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:24.450
Correct, the Militia possesses a girl named Kihel who's virtually indistinguishable from Queen Dianna.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.120
And the real one fled to Mistletoe?

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:28.250
Yes.

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:32.830
Yo! Did you enjoy visiting Earth?

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:38.260
Yes! For Her Majesty Dianna's sake, I would like to borrow a ship.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:41.050
A vessel, did you say?

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:44.640
I have just now escaped from the Militia's ship. We must hurry.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:50.430
The Militia has gathered here within Mistletoe. We should destroy them now before...

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:53.150
Mistletoe isn't what's important right now.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:57.150
Since you originally disagreed with me over the Earth Immigration plan...

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:00.530
You're free to laugh at my circumstances if you please.

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:02.240
I won't mock you.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:05.450
However, I cannot allow one from Earth to use the Queen's name.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:07.240
If I may...

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:10.830
We don't have time to worry about some prospector's daughter.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:16.130
Are you suggesting it'd take my Mahiroo team too long to capture one single little girl?

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.920
Listen to this, Harry.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:21.550
Mistletoe, our goddess of fertility, has been violated!

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:23.930
I must make amends for this insult!

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:25.050
Queen Dianna...

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.720
So it's not just on Earth.

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:32.430
But those in space have been consumed by their battle instincts as well!? That is indeed a tragedy.

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:38.230
- You must be joking. My family line of soldiers... 
- ...knows only of mock combat up until now!

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:40.650
But should that mean you know how to fight a real war?

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.240
Then it must also be said...

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:48.240
...that you've also made it this far because of Dianna Counter, a civilian force.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:52.250
If it were my decision, I'd invade the entire Earth for you in a single day!

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:58.130
It's nothing like that. I only proposed that we return to the Earth.

00:12:58.130 --> 00:12:59.840
This is bad.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:02.710
What am I supposed to do without my Mahiroo?

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:13.730
It looks like a dead-end, but there's a weird light on the television screen.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:15.350
What is this!?

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.940
Are you part of Mistletoe's maintenance crew?

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:20.820
I am with the Ghingnham division.

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:24.820
If you're here to work on Mistletoe, please give me a hand.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:26.320
Roger!

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:45.920
Our port side should be able to go higher.

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:49.930
I'm glad we've saved a bit of time, but will we be able to get out once we've gotten in?

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:52.220
Who knows.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:55.640
Each major hatch should have 2 exits, but...

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:57.230
And if we can't find any?

00:13:57.230 --> 00:14:01.520
Then we use the Mega Particle Cannons to cut open a new exit.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:04.030
Oh... this ship has a lot of power, doesn't it?

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:06.240
Willgem, I'm reporting in!

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:09.160
The "Armadillo" has returned!

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:27.630
It's better if you remain in this room until we've arrived on the moon.

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:29.050
I understand.

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:29.930
Then...

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:31.720
Harry...

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:35.140
I see now that I may have taken this all too far....

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:40.020
But having realized the consequences, I now only want a single promise from you.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.020
A promise?

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:48.030
If I do lose my life, I wish to die in your arms.

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:51.740
That is a promise I cannot grant.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:53.120
Lieutenant...

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:58.250
Because I cannot guarantee that I will not die before that.

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:00.830
If that happens, then I'll hold you in my arms.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:04.420
And I'll take you back to Queen Dianna, if you wish.

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:10.550
Just grant me this request and I will become a perfect double of Queen Dianna for you.

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:14.850
No. I don't wish to put you in such a dangerous situation again.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:20.640
What?

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:23.650
I'd like for you to see the Mahiroo team's deployment firsthand.

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:29.240
Is this room to your tastes?

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:32.740
I dislike the current combat blackout.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:34.530
I would prefer to have some more light.

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:36.950
Then I shall see that it ends soon.

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:38.540
Be well.

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:43.120
Sweatson, sorry for the delay. Commence operation E Minor.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:44.830
That wait was torture...

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:47.250
Okay, time to go!

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:50.920
Mahiroo troops, time for operation E-Minor!

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:54.930
That's right. Use Operation E Minor to show a true display of the Ghingnham Squadron's fireworks!

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:08.730
I'm not seeing any spacecraft around here.

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:10.440
They must be near.

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.320
Perhaps if we knew what was happening outside?

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:15.320
Maybe your unit has access to more confidential data, Cancer?

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.530
There's a system map for Mistletoe...

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:20.120
But I doubt their formation deployment plans would be in here.

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:23.120
Muron, is Dianna still safe there?

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:26.130
You have no right to address her name so casually!

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:28.340
Miss Sochie is here as well, right?

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.840
Thank you all. You've helped me so much.

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:34.630
No kidding. Without us, you probably would've gotten yourself killed.

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:37.350
Hey little lady, I could say the same about you!

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:42.730
I'm a Terran. Shouldn't we expect you Moonrace people to do better than me in space?

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:44.520
I've reached the Willgame!

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.650
Do you read me, Laura?

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.940
Have you found Dianna Soriel?

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:50.730
I have.

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:56.450
I'm sorry my willful actions caused the Militia so much trouble.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:59.450
Nonsense. People help one another at sea.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.120
Space is no different.

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:02.330
Sir Guin!

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:04.910
Miashei brought back this pilot.

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:06.920
If you can view us not as your enemy...

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:10.750
But as the ones who saved your life, we'd appreciate it.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:12.550
What is your name and unit position?

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:14.420
Gym Ghingnham squadron.

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:17.720
Mahiroo team pilot, Shikinen.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:18.720
That is all.

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:21.720
Do you think you're being cute?

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:24.020
Get away from me!

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:27.730
Don't waste your time resisting!

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:29.150
Drop your weapons!

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:30.520
My Mahiroo was taken.

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:32.820
And I allowed my enemy to capture me.

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:35.030
Therefore, I'm not qualified to survive!

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:39.030
Please forgive me through my death, Gym Ghingnham.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:40.530
Don't be a fool!

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:43.120
Well?

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.750
Is he dead?

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:47.750
He's fine, just knocked out.

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:51.340
Goodness... apologizing by taking his own life...

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:52.420
What is it?

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:55.130
She says we can't use the port.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:59.140
No, it's not that. Mechanical Dolls are flying around outside it.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:02.220
The hatch is moving?

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:05.850
What's happening now? Queen Dianna?

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:11.360
The emergency shutters have begun to activate.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.730
The enemy must have done it!

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:17.320
You're right. It seems they intend to entrap me here.

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:20.240
If we keep going this way, we'll make it to the Willgem...

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:33.340
I only reacted because I didn't want to resort to something that reckless!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:34.550
Forgive me.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:44.220
All units, prepare for mechanical doll combat!

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:48.230
That should do.

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:51.350
Laura, it looks like we'll have to meet outside the structure.

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:54.520
Roger that, but will you be able to get out?

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:57.940
If need be, we'll use the Mega Particle Cannon.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.240
Is that alright?

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.450
Can't go that route...

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:03.530
And your end?

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:05.240
It looks like we're in the wrong place.

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:06.620
Rocks don't mean a thing!

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:08.040
It's alright, Muron.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:13.040
Save the FLAT's Vibration system for the spots we can use to get out.

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:15.040
Loran, can you take care of the right side?

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:16.250
Sure.

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:19.050
Your Majesty, are you sure about cutting our way out?

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:21.220
It's going to ruin Mistletoe!

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:24.640
Only in the worst case scenario.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.640
We can get out this way!

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:33.650
Listen up!

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:35.940
Commence the E-minor operation!

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:38.230
No need to hold back!

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:50.460
That was no ordinary explosion!

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:03.430
A heavy bombardment...

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:12.230
Not bad. The Mahiroo team's first battle blossoms with fire.

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:17.820
They also gain some valuable combat experience, Lieutenant Harry.

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:20.650
Is this some sort of grudge against Queen Dianna?

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:26.240
The terrans must be crushed. These are the fireworks of a true campaign against the earth.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:31.250
I can tell how much stronger Queen Dianna's become since she left for earth.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:34.250
If that's the case, she'll see the purpose of this battle.

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:50.220
I'm going to use the FLAT's Vibe now!

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:53.640
Not now! There should be a harbor port coming up on the right!

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:55.730
- You okay?
- Yeah.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:02.440
A tiny rocket...?

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:32.850
Our line of contact to the Willgem...

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:34.850
Are we being jammed?

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:38.730
Miashei and the others... did they get out?

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:49.240
Lieutenant Harry, your hot tea is getting cold!

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:52.120
The dream I've waited 3,000 years for is about to become reality!

00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:54.450
We are now entering into a true war.

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:05.340
Thank you very much for agreeing to lend Dianna a ship.

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:12.060
Queen Dianna was...

00:22:15.220 --> 00:22:18.230
Qu...Queen Dianna...

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:20.940
Has my deception gone too far?

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:43.650
<i>A portion of the destroyed asteroid plummets towards the moon.</i>

00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:47.360
<i>The time for me to use the hidden Atomic Bombs has now arrived.</i>

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:51.900
<i>However, a mobile suit causes the White Doll to resonate...</i>

00:23:51.900 --> 00:23:55.780
<i>...ringing like the sound of a bell, while calling the name "Turn A"</i>

00:23:58.040 --> 00:24:02.960
<i>Next Time... on </i>TURN A GUNDAM<i>
The Asteroid's Explosion</i>

00:24:03.370 --> 00:24:05.880
"The wind calls forth the dawn."

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:08.420
<b>The Asteroid's Explosion</b>
